s7-6-p37 = prose (cons "For a process specified to continue without resource failure, the continuing-block premise \(P\) must include a **re-established resource invariant**. For example, fix a live-state bound \(B\), an arena capacity \(K\ge 2B\), and two equal-size semispaces of capacity \(K/2\). At each turn boundary, let \(\mathsf{Live}(s)\le B\), the roots enumerate every reachable retained value, and \(\mathsf{Free}(s)\) contain enough room for the next turn's temporary allocations. Suppose the turn allocates at most \(A\) bytes between collections and collection copies at most \(B\) live bytes; a sufficient capacity condition for this specific schedule is \(K/2\ge B+A\), with collection and root-update correctness supplied by their machine blocks. The one-turn evidence then has the form" nil)
